.TH CHTTP_BASE64_ENCODE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_base64_encode \- base64-encode a buffer (default allocator)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttp.h>

char *chttp_base64_encode(const void *data, size_t len,
                          size_t *out_len);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Static inline wrapper around chttp_base64_encode_mp() with NULL
memory management procedures (uses malloc/free).
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
data     Buffer to encode. May be NULL only if len is 0.
len      Number of bytes in data.
out_len  Optional; receives the length of the returned string
         (excluding the terminating NUL). Pass NULL to ignore.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Newly allocated, NUL-terminated base64 string on success.
NULL on allocation failure, if data is NULL and len is nonzero, or
if len is large enough that the encoded size would overflow size_t.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_base64_encode_mp (3),
.BR chttp_base64_decode (3)
